# IS THE AGREEMENT STAGE KEEPING UP, AND IS IT STILL AS CHEAP AS IT WAS? -- the identity projection's agreement
# phase (services.identity.agreement.AgreementStage), and the staging publisher beside it.
#
#   - `kinowo_worker_identity_agreement_clusters{state}` -- clusters by agreement state, as the last stage run left
#     them; `incomplete` is a cluster whose verdict is still to be read, the backfill's backlog.
#   - `kinowo_worker_identity_agreement_phase_seconds{mode}` / `..._allocated_bytes{mode}` -- every projection's
#     agreement phase, by projection mode (periodic, whole, changed): the "agreement 69.1s/9579MB" of its
#     `identity projection:` log line, as histograms.
#   - `kinowo_worker_identity_staging_dropped_total` -- staging events the publisher let go unwritten.
#   - `kinowo_worker_identity_model_held_listings` / `..._held_oldest_seconds` -- the identity model's input gate
#     (docs/design/identity-structural-fixes.md, fix 1): listings whose newest version waits on its own questions,
#     and how long the oldest has waited; `..._promoted_total{at="bound"}` -- those taken in at its 10-minute bound,
#     unanswered. No replay runs the gate, so only these see it stuck.
#   - `kinowo_worker_identity_model_kept_listings` / `..._present_listings` -- the departed listings the model keeps as
#     inputs beside the billed ones (docs/design/identity-listing-retention.md): the retention window's cost.
#   - `kinowo_worker_identity_projection_seconds` -- the last identity projection's wall clock.
#
# And, in the `identity-model-health` group at the end, whether the model is up and its projection writing: the model's
# take-up failures and rebuilds, the projection's refusals and the drift its hourly reconcile finds.
groups:
  - name: identity-agreement-recorded
    rules:
      # Each hour's median agreement phase per country and mode: what the regressions below compare with its own
      # week, read back through `quantile_over_time` (a histogram's quantile cannot be taken over 7 days of buckets
      # directly without summing a week of rates at every evaluation).
      - record: kinowo:identity_agreement_phase_seconds:p50_1h
        expr: histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (country, mode, le) (rate(kinowo_worker_identity_agreement_phase_seconds_bucket[1h])))
      - record: kinowo:identity_agreement_phase_allocated_bytes:p50_1h
        expr: histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (country, mode, le) (rate(kinowo_worker_identity_agreement_phase_allocated_bytes_bucket[1h])))

  - name: identity-agreement
    rules:
      # THE BACKFILL HAS LEFT CLUSTERS INCOMPLETE FOR SIX HOURS. A healthy backlog drains within a few projections;
      # one that never reaches 0 is a stage reading nothing (an answer store refusing, a budget spent every time).
      # `last_over_time(...[10m])` bridges a worker restart's scrape gap, which would otherwise reset the hold.
      - alert: IdentityAgreementBackfillStalled
        expr: max by (country) (last_over_time(kinowo_worker_identity_agreement_clusters{state="incomplete"}[10m])) > 0
        for: 6h
        labels:
          severity: warning
          domain: identity
        annotations:
          summary: "{{ $labels.country }}: {{ $value }} agreement clusters have stayed incomplete for 6 hours"
          description: >-
            The agreement stage has had clusters with unread verdicts for six hours without draining them. Its
            per-projection progress is in VictoriaLogs `country:<cc> "agreement"`; the worker diagnostics
            dashboard draws the clusters by state.

      # THE MODEL'S INPUT GATE IS STUCK. A held listing waits on its own family questions, venue page and posters, asked
      # ahead of the agreement's queue: seconds to minutes (11-07..11-11: the oldest under 300 s, the hour's p99 under
      # 5 min). ModelInputGate.MaxHold takes any listing in at 10 min, so one held past 15 min is the bound itself not
      # working (11-06, the gate's first day: 3.6 h, before the bound held) -- and more than 1,000 held at once (a day's
      # arrivals in DE) is a queue not served. Either way listings are shown on their old version, or a new one not at
      # all, for as long as it lasts. `max_over_time(...[10m])` bridges a restart's gap and skips the NaN a restart seeds
      # these gauges with until the gate first measures them. The agreement stage's previous takes standing while a
      # refreshed answer's questions are checked (AgreementStage.standing, the same 10-minute bound) count in the same
      # gauges and in promoted_total{at="bound"}: this alert and IdentityInputGateWaitsLong page on both.
      - alert: IdentityInputGateStuck
        expr: |
          max by (country) (max_over_time(kinowo_worker_identity_model_held_oldest_seconds[10m])) > 900
          or
          max by (country) (max_over_time(kinowo_worker_identity_model_held_listings[10m])) > 1000
        for: 10m
        labels:
          severity: warning
          domain: identity
        annotations:
          summary: "{{ $labels.country }}: the identity model's input gate holds listings too long or too many ({{ $value }})"
          description: >-
            Listings whose newest version waits on its own questions are held past the gate's 10-minute bound
            (ModelInputGate.MaxHold), or over a thousand are held. Their questions are AskQuestion tasks claimed at 0,
            venue-page reads and poster hashes; the worker diagnostics dashboard's "Identity input gate" panel draws
            the held count, the oldest wait and the promotions. The one switch: IdentityModelService.NewWhilePending.

      # THE GATE'S WAITS RUN TO ITS BOUND. A listing taken in at ModelInputGate.MaxHold (`promoted_total{at="bound"}`)
      # waited 10 minutes on a question none of its attempts concluded: a host answering nothing, a poster fetch hanging,
      # a question kind the queue does not claim ahead. None since 11-06 (the gate's first day); three in an hour is a
      # pattern, not one slow host -- each such listing is taken in on what it has and its take can move when the
      # answer comes (the flips the gate is there to stop).
      - alert: IdentityInputGateWaitsLong
        expr: sum by (country) (increase(kinowo_worker_identity_model_promoted_total{at="bound"}[1h])) >= 3
        labels:
          severity: warning
          domain: identity
        annotations:
          summary: "{{ $labels.country }}: {{ $value | printf \"%.0f\" }} listings waited the input gate's full 10 minutes in the last hour"
          description: >-
            The identity model's input gate took listings in at its 10-minute bound, their questions unanswered. The
            worker logs "held listing(s) taken in past the 10 min bound" (VictoriaLogs `country:<cc> "past the"`);
            the questions are in identity_family_answers and the AskQuestion tasks. Look for the family, host or
            poster that stopped answering.

      # THE KEPT LISTINGS OUTNUMBER THE BILLED ONES. A departed listing stays an input while a billed one relates to it by
      # title (ListingRetention), up to the retention window: measured 2026-11-07, DE kept 830 more listings per day of
      # departures (+23% of the 32.5k billed after 9 days), so the window's cost grows with the store's history. Past 1x
      # the billed set the resolve reads twice its population: look at the window before raising it, or lower it. Read
      # through max/min_over_time, which skip a restart's NaN seed, so the hour's hold bridges a restart.
      - alert: IdentityKeptListingsHigh
        expr: |
          max by (country) (max_over_time(kinowo_worker_identity_model_kept_listings[15m]))
            > max by (country) (min_over_time(kinowo_worker_identity_model_present_listings[15m]))
        for: 1h
        labels:
          severity: warning
          domain: identity
        annotations:
          summary: "{{ $labels.country }}: the identity model keeps {{ $value }} departed listings, more than it bills"
          description: >-
            The departed listings kept as identity inputs (ListingRetention, identity_retained) outnumber the billed
            ones, so every family's resolve reads at least twice its population. The window is ListingRetention's
            grace (docs/design/identity-listing-retention.md); the worker diagnostics dashboard draws kept, departed and
            billed listings beside the projection's seconds.

      # THE PROJECTION TAKES A QUARTER LONGER THAN A WEEK AGO. The last six hours' mean wall clock against the same six
      # hours a week before, above 30 s (a scoped projection takes seconds: a quarter of that is noise). What a growing
      # kept set costs shows here first; a deploy that slows the resolver too. Not in the hour after a worker start.
      - alert: IdentityProjectionSlower
        expr: |
          (
            avg by (country) (avg_over_time(kinowo_worker_identity_projection_seconds[6h]))
              > 1.25 * avg by (country) (avg_over_time(kinowo_worker_identity_projection_seconds[6h] offset 7d))
            and
            avg by (country) (avg_over_time(kinowo_worker_identity_projection_seconds[6h])) > 30
          )
          unless on (country)
          (time() - max by (country) (last_over_time(process_start_time_seconds{job="kinowo-worker"}[10m]))) < 3600
        for: 1h
        labels:
          severity: warning
          domain: identity
        annotations:
          summary: "{{ $labels.country }}: identity projections average {{ $value | humanizeDuration }} over 6h, a quarter slower than a week ago"
          description: >-
            The identity projection's mean wall clock over the last six hours is over 1.25x the same window a week ago.
            Compare kinowo_worker_identity_model_kept_listings with the billed listings (a longer retention window
            costs resolve time), then the builds deployed between: VictoriaLogs `country:<cc> "identity projection:"`.

      # THE AGREEMENT PHASE COSTS TWICE ITS WEEK. The hour's median wall clock above twice the week's median of that
      # hourly median, and above 20 s (a scoped projection's phase is about a second: doubling it is noise). Not in
      # the hour after a worker start: a deploy's first projection is a whole one and runs cold. The 10-minute hold
      # also lets that projection's sample leave the 1h window before anything can fire.
      - alert: IdentityAgreementCostRegression
        expr: |
          (
            kinowo:identity_agreement_phase_seconds:p50_1h
              > 2 * quantile_over_time(0.5, kinowo:identity_agreement_phase_seconds:p50_1h[7d])
            and
            kinowo:identity_agreement_phase_seconds:p50_1h > 20
          )
          unless on (country)
          (time() - max by (country) (last_over_time(process_start_time_seconds{job="kinowo-worker"}[10m]))) < 3600
        for: 10m
        labels:
          severity: warning
          domain: identity
        annotations:
          summary: "{{ $labels.country }}: the {{ $labels.mode }} agreement phase's hourly median is {{ $value | humanizeDuration }}, over twice its week"
          description: >-
            The identity projection's agreement phase has doubled its weekly median. Find the build and the
            projections: VictoriaLogs `country:<cc> "identity projection:"`, whose phase list names each phase's
            seconds and MB; the worker diagnostics dashboard draws the hour against the week.

      # THE SAME, FOR WHAT IT ALLOCATES: steadier than the wall clock, which CPU contention on the node moves, and the
      # first to show a change that copies a corpus per verdict. Floor 2 GB.
      - alert: IdentityAgreementAllocationRegression
        expr: |
          (
            kinowo:identity_agreement_phase_allocated_bytes:p50_1h
              > 2 * quantile_over_time(0.5, kinowo:identity_agreement_phase_allocated_bytes:p50_1h[7d])
            and
            kinowo:identity_agreement_phase_allocated_bytes:p50_1h > 2e9
          )
          unless on (country)
          (time() - max by (country) (last_over_time(process_start_time_seconds{job="kinowo-worker"}[10m]))) < 3600
        for: 10m
        labels:
          severity: warning
          domain: identity
        annotations:
          summary: "{{ $labels.country }}: the {{ $labels.mode }} agreement phase's hourly median allocation is {{ $value | humanize }}B, over twice its week"
          description: >-
            The identity projection's agreement phase allocates twice its weekly median. VictoriaLogs
            `country:<cc> "identity projection:"` names each projection's phases with their MB; compare the
            build before and after.

      # A STAGING EVENT WAS DROPPED. The staging publisher let a take change or a wait go unwritten: the local
      # /debug/identity/staging page misses it. Zero always; the counter is seeded at 0 per country.
      - alert: IdentityStagingEventsDropped
        expr: sum by (country) (increase(kinowo_worker_identity_staging_dropped_total[30m])) > 0
        labels:
          severity: warning
          domain: identity
        annotations:
          summary: "{{ $labels.country }}: the identity staging publisher dropped events"
          description: >-
            Identity staging events (take changes, waits) were let go before a publish wrote them -- the feed let
            them go, or publishes kept failing -- so the staging screen misses them. VictoriaLogs
            `country:<cc> "identity staging"` has the WARN line per drop and the failed publishes before it.

  # IS THE IDENTITY MODEL UP, AND IS ITS PROJECTION WRITING? -- the incremental model (IdentityModelService) and the
  # projection it feeds (IdentityProjection). Each of these counters is 0 on a healthy worker and seeded at 0 per
  # country from boot, so increase() sees the first one and bridges a restart's reset. Over 2026-11-04..18 they counted:
  # take-up failures none; rebuilds one (UK 11-16 23:45, a single drain that failed and rebuilt cleanly); refusals two
  # bursts (UK `shrink` x3 on 11-09 18:45, UK `failed` x1 on 11-17 08:40), each followed by written projections;
  # drift none. Every rule below asks for a REPEAT, so each of those one-offs stays quiet.
  - name: identity-model-health
    rules:
      # THE MODEL CANNOT BE TAKEN UP. A failed take-up leaves the model DOWN (`model = None`) and retries it after 1, 2,
      # 4 ... up to 30 minutes. While it is down nothing drains: no scrape reaches identity, every projection is
      # refused `notready`, and the site serves the films as they were when it went down -- new films never appear.
      # One failure the first retry answers is a blip (a Mongo read timing out at boot); a SECOND within the hour is
      # the retry failing too. Pipeline, not identity: this is the scrape-to-site path stopped, not a take's quality.
      - alert: IdentityModelTakeUpFailing
        expr: sum by (country) (increase(kinowo_worker_identity_model_takeup_failures_total[1h])) >= 2
        labels:
          severity: warning
          domain: pipeline
        annotations:
          summary: "{{ $labels.country }}: the identity model failed {{ $value | printf \"%.0f\" }} take-ups in the last hour"
          description: >-
            IdentityModelService could not take its model up from its store, and the retry failed too, so the model is
            down: no scrape is drained into identity and every projection is refused (`notready`) -- the site keeps
            serving the films as they were, and no new film reaches it. The worker logs "identity model: take-up
            failed" with the exception, and "identity model: down -- take-up retried in Ns" (VictoriaLogs
            `country:<cc> "identity model:"`). Usually the identity store's read (Mongo, a decode); the retry backs off
            to 30 minutes, so once the cause is fixed a worker restart takes it up at once.

      # THE MODEL KEEPS REBUILDING. A drain that throws rebuilds the whole model from its store (`safely`): minutes on
      # US, during which nothing drains. One is the backstop working (UK 11-16). Three in an hour is a drain that fails
      # every time it runs -- the model spends its time rebuilding, and listings reach the site only between rebuilds.
      - alert: IdentityModelRebuildLoop
        expr: sum by (country) (increase(kinowo_worker_identity_model_rebuilds_total[1h])) > 2
        labels:
          severity: warning
          domain: pipeline
        annotations:
          summary: "{{ $labels.country }}: the identity model rebuilt itself {{ $value | printf \"%.0f\" }} times in the last hour"
          description: >-
            Drains of the incremental identity model keep throwing, and each one rebuilds the model from its store, so
            scrapes are taken into identity late or not at all. The worker logs "identity model: <what> failed --
            rebuilding from its store" with the exception (VictoriaLogs `country:<cc> "rebuilding from its store"`):
            the same <what> and exception every time is one input the drain cannot take -- find the listing or event
            it names. A "rebuild failed" after it also counts in IdentityModelTakeUpFailing.

      # THE PROJECTION KEEPS BEING REFUSED. A refused projection writes nothing and the stored films keep serving --
      # right for one bad run, and identity frozen in silence when every run is refused: new films do not appear,
      # moved takes do not move. Refused in every hour's window for two hours (the hourly whole-corpus projection
      # alone keeps the window full when it is the one refused), so a burst -- UK's three `shrink`s on 11-09 -- holds
      # the condition for an hour and stays quiet.
      - alert: IdentityProjectionRefusing
        expr: sum by (country) (increase(kinowo_worker_identity_projection_refusals_total[1h])) > 0
        for: 2h
        labels:
          severity: warning
          domain: pipeline
        annotations:
          summary: "{{ $labels.country }}: identity projections have been refused for two hours ({{ $value | printf \"%.0f\" }} in the last hour)"
          description: >-
            Every hour for two hours the identity projection was refused, so nothing it resolved has been written: the
            site serves the films as they stood before, new films do not appear and corrected takes do not land. The
            `reason` label of kinowo_worker_identity_projection_refusals_total says which guard: `shrink`
            (ProjectionGuard: the projection would drop too large a share of films -- a scrape that came back empty, or
            a resolver change), `crossing` (a family crossing), `unreadablemap` (the FilmId map could not be read),
            `notready` (the model is down: see IdentityModelTakeUpFailing) or `failed` (it threw). Each refusal logs
            "identity projection refused (<reason>): <why>" (VictoriaLogs `country:<cc> "identity projection
            refused"`); `failed` logs "identity projection failed" with the stack trace.

      # A SCOPED PROJECTION MISSED FILMS, AGAIN. Between hourly whole-corpus projections the worker projects only the
      # films a change reaches (ProjectionScope); the hourly one counts the films it changed that those scopes should
      # have (`drift_total`) and puts them right. One drifting reconcile is a film stale for under an hour and a scope
      # bug worth a look; drift in TWO reconciles running (the 70-minute window bridges the hour's jitter, so one
      # holds it 70 minutes and two 130) is a scope that keeps missing. None in 2026-11-04..18.
      - alert: IdentityProjectionDrifting
        expr: sum by (country) (increase(kinowo_worker_identity_projection_drift_total[70m])) > 0
        for: 90m
        labels:
          severity: warning
          domain: identity
        annotations:
          summary: "{{ $labels.country }}: hourly identity projections keep finding films the scoped ones missed ({{ $value | printf \"%.0f\" }})"
          description: >-
            Two or more hourly whole-corpus identity projections running changed films that the scoped projections
            between them (ProjectionScope: only the films a change reaches) left as they were, so those films were
            served stale for up to an hour each time. The reconcile has put each right; the bug is in the scope -- a
            change whose reach ProjectionScope does not follow. The projection's log line names the drifted films
            (VictoriaLogs `country:<cc> "identity projection drift"`); reproduce one with scripts/identity-slice.
